&lt;h3&gt;About This Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building our enrichment facilities and the high-density computing infrastructure behind them. We&#39;re hiring an Electrical Engineer to own power distribution inside the rack. You&#39;ll define how power gets from the facility tap-off to every server PSU in our high-density racks. That means selecting PDUs and power shelves, laying out busbars, assigning outlets and phases, and making sure every rack stays up when a feed goes down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on design role, not a specification-only role. We want someone who has designed rack power, tested it, found the problems, and fixed them. You&#39;ll be the technical authority on rack power and the bridge between our facility electrical team and our IT hardware team. You&#39;ll set the technical foundation for work of lasting national importance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you seek high impact and are excited by fast-paced, intense, Skunkworks-style projects, we encourage you to apply to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rack Power Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the rack power architecture end to end, from busway tap-off or RPP through rack PDUs, in-rack busbars, and power shelves to server PSUs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define rack power topologies for high-density AI/GPU and HPC deployments (50–130+ kW per rack), including 48V/54V busbar (OCP ORv3) and liquid-cooled configurations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set redundancy strategy at the rack level (A/B feeds, PSU N+1 and N+N) and verify failure-mode loading under single-feed operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detailed Design &amp;amp; Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select and specify rack PDUs (metered, switched, intelligent), power shelves, BBUs, and power cords and whips (IEC C13/C19/C20, IEC 60309, NEMA L21)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce rack elevations with power assignments, outlet-level load schedules, and phase-balance calculations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze inrush current, hold-up time, breaker coordination at the branch and rack level, voltage drop, and connector and busbar thermal loading&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Size branch circuits, tap-offs, and RPP circuits feeding each rack, and set derating and power-capping strategy for variable GPU workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integration &amp;amp; Validation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with server OEMs, ODMs, and PDU and power shelf vendors on design reviews, submittals, and technical issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with facility electrical, mechanical/liquid cooling, controls, and IT hardware teams to resolve rack-to-facility interface issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead rack power validation through lab testing, factory integration, and on-site commissioning, and drive root cause on any power issue found&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate rack power monitoring (intelligent PDUs, branch circuit monitoring) with DCIM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Control&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare design packages that move through formal engineering review, configuration management, and change control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with NEC (NFPA 70), NFPA 70E, NFPA 75, applicable IEEE standards, and UL/IEC listing requirements for rack equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Electrical Engineering or a closely related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[5+] years of electrical design experience, with at least [3] years designing power distribution at the rack and server level for data center or hyperscale deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct design experience with rack PDUs, in-rack busbars, power shelves, or server power delivery, not only facility-level MEP design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of A/B redundancy, phase balancing, branch circuit sizing, inrush, and PSU redundancy behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking rack power designs through testing, integration, or commissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency producing rack elevations, load schedules, and one-line diagrams (AutoCAD, Revit, Visio, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be a U.S. person (export control requirement) and able to obtain and maintain a U.S. government security clearance [FSO to confirm wording]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Skills and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-density AI/GPU racks such as NVIDIA GB200/GB300 NVL72, MGX, or comparable platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OCP Open Rack (ORv3), 48V/54V busbar, BBU systems, or emerging higher-voltage DC rack architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liquid-cooled rack integration experience (power and cooling interface, CDU and manifold coordination)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background on a hyperscaler hardware team, AI rack integrator, ODM, or rack PDU or power shelf manufacturer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with facility-side distribution (busway, RPPs, UPS) and power system tools (ETAP, SKM, EasyPower)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer (PE) license&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a regulated industry (nuclear, aerospace, defense, pharma) with formal design control or QA programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Additional Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work extended hours and weekends as necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
