&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an embedded software engineer to design and develop firmware for the safety-critical electromechanical systems in service of our mission. The role is hands-on and covers the whole embedded stack. You&#39;ll bring up new boards, write drivers, design portable hardware abstraction layers and build the hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) infrastructure that tests every change on real hardware. You’ll make important system level decisions that impact other teams. Because these systems are safety-critical, you&#39;ll think carefully about how they can fail. You will help solve challenging engineering problems by contributing code with a heavy emphasis on efficiency and safety. You&#39;ll work closely with electrical and controls engineers: reviewing boards, turning control requirements into firmware and debugging on the bench. As a member of a growing team, you&#39;ll also help set the engineering standards others build on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop bare-metal, safety-critical software in modern C++ that is readable, testable and efficient.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring up new boards and debug board-level issues with oscilloscopes, logic analyzers and other lab equipment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write drivers for a range of ICs over UART, SPI and I2C.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain wired communication stacks, e.g. CANopen,&amp;nbsp;TCP, UDP&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Design HAL interfaces that let applications move between platforms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use MCU peripherals to enforce safety at the hardware level and make applications more efficient.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze how electromechanical systems and your software can fail together and work to mitigate the effects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build HIL CI infrastructure that tests software changes on real hardware.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally with engineers across multiple disciplines (electrical, mechanical, software)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present firmware designs to stakeholders to keep all engineering disciplines aligned.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, design reviews, and failure mode analysis reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or a related field&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional embedded software development experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong production experience in modern C++ or Rust&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience integrating hardware and software and developing device drivers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable reading schematics and datasheets and debugging on the bench&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience implementing wired communication stacks such as CANopen, TCP, and UDP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience designing bootloaders and firmware update mechanisms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience leading bring-up of new boards&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience writing firmware for closed-loop control systems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
