&lt;h3&gt;About the Company&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;General Matter enriches uranium.&lt;br&gt;We are designing, building, and operating the world&#39;s lowest-cost enrichment services, here in the US.&lt;br&gt;In the process, we are restoring America&#39;s ability to produce nuclear fuel to power AI, advanced manufacturing and critical industries our country relies on to remain competitive.&lt;br&gt;Fuel drives the cost of advanced reactor electricity production, and enrichment drives the cost of the fuel that advanced reactors consume. Reliable, low-cost enrichment is the catalyst for the nuclear Renaissance now under way.&lt;br&gt;Our mission is to make nuclear not only the cleanest and safest source of baseload power, but also the most affordable. We believe abundant nuclear energy will lead to a post-scarcity society.&lt;br&gt;We were incubated inside Founders Fund, like Anduril and Palantir before us, and are backed by over a dozen of the world&#39;s top venture capital firms.&lt;br&gt;Our lean, world-class team of engineers and operators is applying a first-principles approach to solving the problem of nuclear fuel production.&lt;br&gt;We are a mission-driven company with a culture of urgency, accountability, and transparency.&lt;br&gt;Help us build a high-energy society by making the cleanest, safest form of baseload energy the most affordable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About This Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Fluid Systems Engineer at General Matter, you are the Responsible Engineer for the fluid systems that move, store, and control the process fluids at the heart of our enrichment facility.&amp;nbsp;You will set requirements and operating margins, choose the architecture, design and analyze the hardware, lead the first-article build, qualify it, and define how it is commissioned and operated. This is a rare chance to own operation-critical hardware end-to-end at a next-generation nuclear facility during rapid commercial scale-up, on work of national importance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you seek high impact and ownership, and are excited by fast-paced, intense, Skunkworks-style projects, we encourage you to apply to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the fluid system requirements: perform system-level sizing and performance analysis to establish requirements and operating margins and carry them through the life of the hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design pressurized and unpressurized components and assemblies, producing original CAD models, drawings, and specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structural, mechanical, and thermal analysis to ensure survivability under pressure, thermal, and operational loads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the design owner for fluid hardware in the facility safety basis, supporting the Integrated Safety Analysis and the safety functions of any IROFS your systems provide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal and external design reviews with cross-functional partners, suppliers, and stakeholders, and defend your design and your data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive design-for-manufacturability improvements to enable efficient, repeatable production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead first-article builds and work directly with manufacturing teams to establish robust production processes and stay with the hardware through production ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute development, qualification, and acceptance testing for critical hardware, and own the results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the concept of operations for your systems, from commissioning and acceptance testing through steady-state operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your systems after they are running: resolve nonconformances, drive design changes through change control, and feed operational lessons back into the next design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of exceptional ability (prior projects, portfolio of work, completed products, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (or higher) in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Engineering Physics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;+2-5 years of experience designing, analyzing, or testing fluid systems (e.g., pressurized systems, piping/tubing, valves, pumps, or related hardware)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain required security clearance and access authorization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Skills and Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning operation-critical hardware from concept through production, ideally as a Responsible Engineer or equivalent single point of accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with gas dynamics, thermal analysis, and finite element analysis (FEA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with pressurized systems (e.g., valves, regulators, piping, tubing, pressure vessels), though not limited to them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with FEA tools and CAD software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced, resource-constrained environments such as early-stage hardware, new-space, or defense hard-tech companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with nuclear, DOE, national lab, or NRC-licensed facilities, or with other regulated, safety-critical systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across disciplines with manufacturing, safety, and operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, organization, and technical leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Additional Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work extended hours and weekends as necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
