&lt;p&gt;Help us build a high-energy society by making the cleanest, safest form of baseload energy the most affordable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Lead Embedded Software Engineer to design and develop firmware for the safety-critical electromechanical systems in service of our mission, and to lead the growing team that builds it. The role is hands-on and covers the whole embedded stack. You&#39;ll bring up new boards, write drivers, design portable hardware abstraction layers and build the hardware-in-the-loop (HIL) infrastructure that tests every change on real hardware. You&#39;ll set the technical direction and architecture for our embedded software and make system-level decisions that shape how other teams design and build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because these systems are safety-critical, you&#39;ll think carefully about how they can fail, and you&#39;ll make sure your team does too. Much of your time will go to writing code and solving challenging engineering problems, with a heavy emphasis on efficiency and safety. You&#39;ll work closely with electrical and controls engineers: reviewing boards, turning control requirements into firmware architecture and debugging on the bench. You&#39;ll also mentor engineers and set the bar for how the team designs, reviews and tests firmware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop bare-metal, safety-critical software in modern C++ that is readable, testable and efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring up new boards and debug board-level issues with oscilloscopes, logic analyzers and other lab equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write drivers for a range of ICs over UART, SPI and I2C.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain wired communication stacks, e.g. CANopen, TCP, UDP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design HAL interfaces that let applications move between platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use MCU peripherals to enforce safety at the hardware level and make applications more efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze how electromechanical systems and your software can fail together and work to mitigate the effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build HIL CI infrastructure that tests software changes on real hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally with engineers across multiple disciplines (electrical, mechanical, software)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present firmware designs to stakeholders to keep all engineering disciplines aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, design reviews, and failure mode analysis reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical and architectural leadership based on first principles thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
