&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mechanical Engineer, you will play a pivotal role in executing a state-of-the-art enrichment facility from concept through commissioning. You will design, analyze, and ensure mechanical designs meet regulatory requirements for safety, performance, and compliance. You will have the opportunity to work on a greenfield project collaborating with structural engineers, electrical engineers, architects, and both internal and external partners to develop detailed mechanical designs and specifications. You will wear multiple hats and supporting your design work through vendor activity and troubleshooting. This is an exciting opportunity to solve complex problems at scale, manage multiple projects in a dynamic environment, and bring modern enrichment facilities online.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design and analysis of mechanical systems including HVAC systems, central plant design (chillers, boilers, heat exchangers), and distribution sizing (ductwork, piping).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare design packages up to Permit level in Revit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with structural, architectural, electrical, and chemical engineers to design and integrate safe and performant mechanical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and review code-compliant designs up to permit level, create comprehensive drawing sets (Revit/AutoCAD), and produce calculations, specifications, and technical reports for design validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to project concept development, feasibility studies, and scope definition, delivering mechanical solutions that meet performance, cost, and schedule goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in mechanical engineering or similar discipline.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of industry experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer (PE) license is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with HVAC systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in AutoCAD, Revit, and Bluebeam.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours and weekends as necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of exceptional ability (prior projects, portfolio of work, completed products, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced engineering environment or a highly technical role requiring a resourceful, entrepreneurial approach to complete tasks within tight timeframes or budget constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of power coordination and arc flash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a consulting firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computational fluids knowledge (CFD) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing custom details to support unique facility design conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on large scale, mission critical construction projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with local/state code compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
