&lt;p&gt;Help us build a high-energy society by making the cleanest, safest form of baseload energy the most affordable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The NDT Technician is responsible for performing nondestructive testing examinations, interpreting and evaluating results, preparing written NDT reports, and developing NDT procedures and work instructions. This position requires certification in one or more NDT methods and demonstrated experience in technical writing for NDT procedures in accordance with applicable codes and standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain NDT procedures, techniques, and work instructions in accordance with applicable codes, standards, specifications, and quality requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform NDT examinations, interpret and evaluate results, and prepare clear, accurate inspection reports and supporting documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development and qualification of WPSs and PQRs, including weld process qualification and evaluation of new welding processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret applicable construction, welding, fabrication, and inspection codes to establish appropriate examination and acceptance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop inspection methodologies and support production troubleshooting, root-cause investigations, and resolution of weld and fabrication quality issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineering, manufacturing, welding, and quality teams while providing technical guidance and mentorship to NDT personnel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
