&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Specialist Lab Piping Designer to lead the design of complex fluid and gas distribution systems for our most sensitive R&amp;amp;D, industrial, and high-stakes infrastructure projects. This role sits at the intersection of process engineering and architectural coordination, requiring a designer who understands that a wet lab or a cleanroom is only as functional as the high-purity systems supporting it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for architecting the routing, containment, and point-of-use delivery for specialized gases and high-purity water systems. Working within our Facility Design team, you will ensure that hazardous and inert gases, vacuum systems, and ultra-pure liquids are integrated seamlessly into the building’s structural and mechanical fabric, adhering to the highest standards of safety and contamination control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and engineer comprehensive laboratory piping systems, including high-purity specialty gases such as N2, compressed air, vacuum, and RODI (Reverse Osmosis/Deionized) water systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare high-fidelity design packages in Revit, owning the 3D coordination of sloped waste lines, gas manifolds, and overhead service carriers within complex ceiling voids.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specify materials and components appropriate for the medium, ranging from orbitally welded stainless steel for high-purity gases to acid-resistant neutralized waste piping for wet labs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop P&amp;amp;IDs (Piping and Instrumentation Diagrams) and flow schematics that define system logic, pressure regulation, and emergency shut-off protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multidisciplinary coordination to ensure piping routes do not conflict with structural bracing, HVAC ductwork, or electrical busways, maintaining strict architectural clearances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure code compliance with NFPA 45 (Standard on Fire Protection for Laboratories using Chemicals), NFPA 99 (Health Care Facilities Code), and ASME B31.3 (Process Piping).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support construction and commissioning by performing submittal reviews and technical field inspections to verify the integrity of specialized joints and purges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Architectural Engineering, or Architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in specialized piping design for R&amp;amp;D, healthcare, or semiconductor facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Revit and AutoCAD, specifically in creating parametric pipe types and complex 3D assemblies for laboratory equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical knowledge of laboratory-grade plumbing, gas cabinet integration, and high-purity water generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, balancing the precision of micro-level piping details with the scale of massive industrial facility design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional Engineer (PE) or AIA license is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BIM automation (Dynamo or Python) to streamline pipe routing and automated pressure drop calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in nuclear or pharmaceutical environments, where containment and high-integrity piping are mission-critical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with seismic bracing for piping systems in high-seismic zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to translate complex P&amp;amp;IDs into clear architectural layouts for project stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why General Matter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale: Work on specialized systems for a massive, first-of-its-kind enrichment facility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complexity: Solve the unique challenges of routing hazardous and high-purity media in a high-security industrial context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovation: Join a team that values digital engineering and &quot;hands-on&quot; technical excellence from design through construction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
