&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a General Matter Information Technology Intern, you will gain hands-on experience supporting the IT systems, infrastructure, and end-user services that keep a highly regulated, mission-critical environment running. You will work alongside experienced IT and security staff on real projects spanning systems administration, network support, endpoint management, and IT compliance. You&#39;ll work closely with cross-functional teams, including electrical engineers, software engineers, chemical engineers, manufacturing engineers, nuclear engineers, materials scientists, and physicists. This is an opportunity to gain meaningful experience supporting the technology backbone of a company advancing domestic nuclear fuel production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with day-to-day IT support, including hardware/software troubleshooting, account provisioning, and helpdesk ticket resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the administration and maintenance of endpoints, servers, and network infrastructure, including patching, backups, and asset tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help implement and validate IT security controls (e.g., MFA, endpoint protection, access management) under the guidance of the IT and security teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support user access reviews, system health checks, and IT policy compliance activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal documentation, including setup guides, runbooks, and IT knowledge base articles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with onboarding/offboarding workflows, equipment deployment, and conference room / office technology support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in IT projects such as software rollouts, systems migrations, and process automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit and compliance readiness efforts by organizing documentation and assisting with internal IT reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current undergraduate or graduate student pursuing a degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundational understanding of computer systems, networking, and IT operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and a willingness to learn new technologies and methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team member who thrives in fast-paced, multidisciplinary environments and is eager to learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with IT service management tools, ticketing systems, or asset management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to scripting or automation tools (e.g., Python, PowerShell).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework or project experience with systems administration, networking, or cloud platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with basic security principles such as authentication, access control, and endpoint protection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
