&lt;p&gt;Help us build a high-energy society by making the cleanest, safest form of baseload energy the most affordable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Manufacturing Engineer Intern, you will gain hands-on experience developing the manufacturing processes, tools, and systems that help take new hardware from development into production. You will work alongside design and manufacturing engineers to improve the safety, performance, cost, and manufacturability of parts, systems, and assemblies. You’ll spend time on the shop floor assembling hardware and test stands, troubleshooting problems, and iterating on processes based on what you learn. This is an opportunity to build practical manufacturing experience while contributing to highly reliable systems and helping drive down the cost of enrichment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement scalable manufacturing processes to ensure reliable, safe systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with design engineers and make recommendation for improved manufacturability, performance, safety, and cost.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, assemble, and validate prototypes, test stands, and development units.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform root-cause analysis on test failures and develop hardware mitigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish manufacturing and quality practices that scale with the company and through production phases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
