&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a Bachelor’s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field (Junior or Senior standing preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completed coursework in HVAC design, heat transfer, thermodynamics, and fluid hydraulics/dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic familiarity with BIM modeling software, such as Revit and AutoCAD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in IES software or energy analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and/or experience in AI tools for design, visual programming (Dynamo, Grasshopper), coding (Python, C#), and/or open-source projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset and a demonstrated interest in the built environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate thoughts and technical ideas in an accessible, collaborative manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
